<p><%= @emails.length > 1 ? "Hi all," : "Hi there," %></p>

<p>
  <%= @whodunnit.name %> <%= "(an #{@is_manager ? "organization manager" : "Fuime admin"})" unless @whodunnit == User.system_user %> has enabled monthly announcements for <%= @event.name %>.
  <%# FUIME-DIVERGENCE: "our blog post" linked to blog.hcb.hackclub.com — Fuime
      calling Hack Club's blog its own, in an email to a Fuime user. Fuime has no
      blog, so the sentence explains itself instead. %>
  This automatically writes an announcement each month and sends it to your followers.
</p>

<p>
  <%# "donations" was HCB's money-in. Fuime's is sales — Fuime::DisabledModules
      turns donations off entirely, so this described a section that cannot
      appear. %>
  By default each announcement summarises how the business did that month — what it sold and what it spent — and you can edit it to say whatever you like.
  Your first monthly announcement has been generated and is scheduled to be sent on <%= @scheduled_for.strftime("%B #{@scheduled_for.day.ordinalize}") %> - <%= link_to "view or edit it on Fuime", announcement_url(@monthly_announcement) %>!
  If your organization doesn't have any activity from this month to include in the announcement by <%= @warning_date.strftime("%B #{@warning_date.day.ordinalize}") %>, the announcement will not be sent.
</p>

<p>Managers can disable monthly announcements at any time in <%= link_to "your settings", edit_event_url(@event) %>.</p>

<p>
  From,<br>
  The Fuime Team
</p>
